@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Returns";
}

<h1>Start a return</h1>
<p class="lede">
    Check whether we can fix it without a return, or start one straight away.
</p>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Returning an item</h3>
    <p class="muted">
        Enter your serial number and we will check it against your plan. If a quick step fixes
        the problem, we will not make you post anything back.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" asp-controller="RmaWizard" asp-action="Start">Start a return</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>How this works</h3>
    <ol class="steps-list">
        <li>Tell us what you are sending back.</li>
        <li>We check each item against the returns policy.</li>
        <li>We suggest a fix from our support articles if one fits.</li>
        <li>You choose where the replacement goes, and confirm.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">
        Automated troubleshooting can suggest a fix. It cannot approve a return, change a
        price, or decide what you owe. Those come from the returns policy, every time.
    </p>
</div>
